Z||000038||anthony_86gt||06-09-2001||10:36 PM||||I live in Monroe Michigan and I see about 3 or 4 that ar driven around town other than mine.  So not that many.||||reg||3
Z||000039||Jncomutt||06-09-2001||11:00 PM||||Wow, I wish I've seen that many around.  In the 2 years that I've had mine, I've only seen 2 on the road.  One SE and one GT, both the red/maroon color.  I live just outside central CT, and there aren't many around.  Hard to find in junkyards too.  <P>There are only 2 other ones I know of.  One has never moved since I noticed it and it probably wont for it as 3 flat tires and the engine compartment is covered with a ragedy tarp.   Has a cracked winshield and stuck headlights.<P>The other is an 87 SE.  I've seen it move from outside of the garage, but never known it to be on the road.  It does run, I think its more of a collector to the owner however.<P>------------------<BR>17 year old Fierophile<BR>'86 Coupe 160k miles<BR>'84 Mint Beauty 51k and original tires!||||reg||1
Z||000040||84Bill||06-09-2001||11:18 PM||||I went to the south Philly junk yards today to see what I could find. I am very unhappy to report that of the 20 or so yards in the area I found only one very badly beaten notchback. At every yard I went to I asked if they get many in and the answer was no. and when they do, they don't keep them long since there is no demand for parts. I did find another yard that had one but it was not theirs yet. <BR>you see Philly addopted a new policy that if car are abandonded for 30 days the tow it to a yard and after another 30 days it's theirs to keep and dispose of. apparently its a GT I asked if I could have the whole car and the answer was no so I said how about 100% of the parts he scoffed at me and said it aint mine yet but I doubt I'll let you have it that way. that bastard!||||reg||9
